  "notes": [
   "fixed pump: the signal carries the whole idler frequency excursion (+-0.55 GHz = +-4.5 pm at 1.567 um)",
   "DFB seed current tuning ~ 0.5-1 GHz/mA in the thermal regime (ASSUMPTION, laser specific): +-0.5-1 mA at 1-100 kHz; above ~ 100 kHz - 1 MHz the thermal response rolls off and the carrier effect (opposite sign) takes over, so 100 kHz is the practical upper end without a phase modulator; residual amplitude modulation ~ 0.5-1 %/mA",
   "the excursion is < 1 % of the QPM frequency acceptance (> 100 GHz for L <= 50 mm): the idler power stays constant",
   "an EDFA (L-band for 1.567 um) passes the modulation unchanged at these rates"
  ]
